Let $
u : \mathbb{Z}_N ightarrow \mathbb{R}^+$ be any measure. Let $\phi_0,\phi_1,\dots,\phi_{k-1} : \mathbb{Z}_N^{k-1} ightarrow \mathbb{Z}_N$ be functions of $k-1$ variables $y_1,\ldots,y_{k-1}$, such that $\phi_i$ does not depend on $y_i$ for $1 \leq i \leq k-1$. Suppose that $f_0,f_1,\dots,f_{k-1} \in L^1(\Z_N)$ are functions satisfying $|f_i(x)| \leq 
u(x)$ for all $x \in \mathbb{Z}_N$ and for each $i$, $0 \leq i \leq k-1$. For each $0 \leq d \leq k-1$, define the quantities  egin{equation} J_{d} :=   \mathbb{E} igg(\prod_{S \subseteq \{k-d,\dots,k-1\}}  ig(\prod_{i = 0}^{k-d-1} f_i(\phi_i(y^{(S)})) ig)  ig(\prod_{i = k-d}^{k-1} 
u^{1/2}(\phi_i (y^{(S)})) ig)\;  igg| \; y \in \mathbb{Z}_N^{k-1}, y' \in \Z_N^d igg) \end{equation} and  egin{equation} P_d := \mathbb{E} igg( \prod_{S \subseteq \{k-d,\dots,k-1\}} 
u(\phi_{k-d-1}(y^{(S)})) \;  igg| \; y \in \Z_N^{k-1}, y' \in \Z_N^d igg).\end{equation} Then for any $0 \leq d \leq k-2$, we have the inequality  egin{equation} |J_{d}|^2 \leq P_d J_{d+1}. \end{equation}

Finally, we observe that \eqref{dual-bounded} is a consequence of the linear forms condition.  Bounding $F$ by $2 (
u+1)/2 = 2 
u_{1/2}$, it suffices to show that $$ {\mathcal D} 
u_{1/2}(x) \leq 1 + o(1) $$ uniformly in the choice of $x \in \mathbb{Z}_N$.  The left-hand side can be expanded using \eqref{cald} as $$ \E igg( \prod_{\omega \in \{0,1\}^{k-1}: \omega 
eq 0^{k-1}} 
u_{1/2}(x + \omega \cdot h) \;  igg| \;  h \in \mathbb{Z}_N^{k-1}  igg).$$ By the linear forms condition \eqref{lfc} (and Lemma ef{halfway}) this expression is $1 + o(1)$.
